-- Ekwo OS — Papua New Guinea: chart of accounts, journals, taxes and defaults.
--
-- Generated from packs/pg at version 0.1.0, do not edit.
-- Change the pack and run `ekwo pack build pg`; `ekwo pack check --all`
-- refuses a seed that is not the exact output of its pack, and the CI runs it.
--
-- Community pack — not reviewed.
-- Written from:
--   Form G1, Goods and Services Tax Return (effective 24 January 2016, Goods and Services Tax Act 2003 as amended) — lines 1 to 16 in three blocks: output debits (total sales, exempt sales, zero-rated sales, taxable sales divided by eleven), input credits (GST paid on business inputs less the share for exempt sales and private use) and the summary of GST payable or refundable; the notes on the exempt industries, the eight zero-rated sales, cars, the section 65A credit and the sales by province (Papua New Guinea Internal Revenue Commission)
--     https://static.irc.gov.pg/2021/December/h8qIml-media-2018-05-01-G1-Goods-Services-Tax-Return.pdf
--   Fact Sheet, Section 65A of the GST Act, Payment of Tax in Special Cases — GST at a rate of 10 % on goods and services sold and on goods imported, output debit and input credit, a registered person files its return (form G1) by the 21st day of the following month, the G1 example (sales K11,000 including GST, output K1,000, input credit K750, K250 to pay) (Papua New Guinea Internal Revenue Commission)
--     https://static.irc.gov.pg/2021/December/5ExWcL-media-GST-Section-65A-Fact-Sheet.pdf
--   Goods and services tax (GST) in Papua New Guinea, a guide produced by KPMG's Port Moresby office (updated October 2025) — GST at 10 %, registration above K250,000 of taxable supplies in any 12 months, the zero-rated and exempt supplies, monthly returns, import GST at 10 % and the reverse charge on certain supplies from abroad; a professional firm's summary, not an official text (KPMG Papua New Guinea, reproduced by Business Advantage PNG)
--     https://www.businessadvantagepng.com/goods-and-services-tax-gst-in-papua-new-guinea/
--   IAS 1 Presentation of Financial Statements — the statement of financial position and the statement of profit or loss, expenses analysed by nature; no Papua New Guinea text prescribing a layout or a chart of accounts was read (IFRS Foundation)
--     https://www.ifrs.org/issued-standards/list-of-standards/ias-1-presentation-of-financial-statements/
--   Internal Revenue Commission — tax administration portal (forms, guides, public notices of filing deadlines; GST is paid and returns are lodged at the IRC) (Papua New Guinea Internal Revenue Commission)
--     https://www.irc.gov.pg/
--
-- Reference data: `install_country_template()` copies it into a company,
-- nothing here belongs to a company.

